---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import { roles, taskDefinitions, onboardingLabels, reviewLabels, deployLabels } from '../../lib/internship-lab.mjs';
import '../../styles/internship-lab.css';
const title = 'Internship Lab · Make one useful thing';
const description = 'Practice a complete creative workflow: interest draft, onboarding, first assignment, task tracking, review and a human-approved release rehearsal. Browser-only; applications are closed.';
---
<BlockLayout title={title} description={description} author="Codex for PointCast" isolated={true} hideAds={true} showNetworkStrip={false} includeManifest={false} themeColor="#183e32" alternates={[{type: 'application/json', href: '/internship-lab/program.json', title: 'Internship Lab workflow and limitations'}]} jsonLd={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:title,description,url:'https://pointcast.xyz/internship-lab/',learningResourceType:'Interactive educational workflow',isAccessibleForFree:true,dateModified:'2026-10-19'}}>
  <div class="il" id="internship-lab">
    <a class="il-skip" href="#il-workspace">Skip to the workspace</a>
    <nav class="il-nav" aria-label="PointCast lab navigation"><a href="/">PointCast<span> / Internship Lab</span></a><a href="/bot-money/">Money Lab ↗</a></nav>
    <header class="il-hero">
      <div><p class="il-kicker">Learn by making / No. 01</p><h1>One useful thing.<br /><em>All the way through.</em></h1><p class="il-lede">A good first project has a beginning, a small piece of real work, and a handoff someone else can understand. Practice the whole loop here.</p><a class="il-button" href="#il-workspace">Open your workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <aside class="il-route" aria-label="Workflow"><span>THE LOOP</span><ol><li>Choose a direction</li><li>Make a small offer</li><li>Leave evidence</li><li>Ask for human review</li><li>Prepare a careful release</li></ol><p>People set the purpose.<br />Bots can help with the work.<br />People own the decision.</p></aside>
    </header>
    <div class="il-notice"><strong>Practice workspace · applications closed</strong><p>This is an educational rehearsal, not a signup form, internship offer or hiring decision. This lab does not save drafts to browser storage or an account. Clear the draft to reset this page; download it to retain a copy. Browser tab restoration can retain page state. Nothing you type is sent to PointCast. Keep names, contact details and other personal information out.</p></div>
    <section class="il-workspace" id="il-workspace" aria-labelledby="il-workspace-title">
      <header class="il-section-head"><div><p class="il-kicker">Your workbench</p><h2 id="il-workspace-title">From interest to handoff</h2></div><p id="il-progress" class="il-progress" aria-live="polite">Start with a direction.</p></header>
      <noscript><p class="il-notice">JavaScript is needed for task tracking and exports. The assignment and checklists below remain readable. You can copy them into your own document.</p></noscript>
      <div class="il-grid">
        <section class="il-card il-interest" aria-labelledby="il-interest-title"><p class="il-step">01 / Interest draft</p><h3 id="il-interest-title">What do you want to get better at?</h3><label for="il-role">Practice role</label><select id="il-role" data-field="role">{roles.map(role => <option>{role}</option>)}</select><label for="il-goal">One learning goal <small>10–500 characters</small></label><textarea id="il-goal" data-field="goal" rows="3" minlength="10" maxlength="500" placeholder="I want to turn a rough idea into a clear, useful product page."></textarea><label for="il-offer">Working title <small>3–120 characters</small></label><input id="il-offer" data-field="offer" minlength="3" maxlength="120" placeholder="A book-swap poster kit" /><p class="il-small">No account, application or enrollment is created. A role here is a learning interest, not an assignment from PointCast.</p></section>
        <section class="il-card" aria-labelledby="il-onboarding-title"><p class="il-step">02 / Onboarding</p><h3 id="il-onboarding-title">Know the working agreement.</h3><p>Use a small, original project. Ask a person to check the result. Keep the next person in mind.</p><div class="il-checks">{onboardingLabels.map((label, i) => <label><input type="checkbox" data-onboarding={i} /><span>{label}</span></label>)}</div><p class="il-small">Before a real internship starts, PointCast must confirm terms, supervision, eligibility, pay, hours and privacy arrangements. This lab establishes none of those.</p></section>
        <section class="il-card il-wide il-assignment" aria-labelledby="il-assignment-title"><div><p class="il-step">03 / The first assignment</p><h3 id="il-assignment-title">Make one offer someone can understand.</h3><p>Choose an original printable, a useful checklist, or a tightly scoped design service. Define who it helps, what is delivered, what is excluded, and what needs human approval. Start with the free First Offer Kit in the <a href="/bot-money/#first-offer-kit">Money Lab</a>.</p><p class="il-small">Example directions, not client commissions: a book-swap poster, an original activity pack, or clearer product cards. No paid work or publication is promised.</p></div><div class="il-deliverable"><span>YOUR HANDOFF</span><strong>One offer page.<br />One product record.<br />One short test note.</strong><p>Done means someone else can inspect it and knows what happens next.</p></div></section>
        <section class="il-card il-wide" aria-labelledby="il-tasks-title"><p class="il-step">04 / Task board</p><h3 id="il-tasks-title">Keep the work visible.</h3><p class="il-small">Move each task as you work. “Ready for review” is your draft status, not acceptance by a reviewer.</p><div class="il-tasks">{taskDefinitions.map(task => <article class="il-task"><p class="il-task-state" data-task-label={task.id}>To do</p><h4>{task.title}</h4><p>{task.detail}</p><label for={`il-task-${task.id}`}>Task status</label><select id={`il-task-${task.id}`} data-task={task.id}><option value="todo">To do</option><option value="doing">In progress</option><option value="ready">Ready for review</option></select></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="il-card" aria-labelledby="il-submission-title"><p class="il-step">05 / Submission draft</p><h3 id="il-submission-title">Leave evidence, not just a tick.</h3><label for="il-evidence">What did you make and check? <small>30–2,000 characters</small></label><textarea id="il-evidence" data-field="evidence" rows="6" minlength="30" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Describe the artifact, its version, source/rights notes, checks performed, and what still needs a second look."></textarea><label for="il-url">Public artifact URL <small>Optional · https only</small></label><input id="il-url" data-field="artifactUrl" type="url" maxlength="500" placeholder="https://example.com/my-draft" aria-describedby="il-url-help" /><p class="il-small" id="il-url-help">The URL is kept as text. This lab does not visit, upload or verify it. Do not include private access links.</p><p class="il-state" id="il-submission-state">Complete your interest draft, onboarding, tasks and evidence to prepare a local review draft.</p></section>
        <section class="il-card" aria-labelledby="il-review-title"><p class="il-step">06 / Review rehearsal</p><h3 id="il-review-title">A second look makes it useful.</h3><p class="il-small">Practice with a human reviewer, or rehearse the questions yourself. These checks are self-reported and do not authenticate a reviewer.</p><fieldset id="il-review-checks" disabled><legend>Review checklist</legend><div class="il-checks">{reviewLabels.map((label, i) => <label><input type="checkbox" data-review={i} /><span>{label}</span></label>)}</div><label for="il-review-note">Review notes and next changes <small>10–1,000 characters</small></label><textarea id="il-review-note" data-field="reviewNote" rows="3" minlength="10" maxlength="1000"></textarea></fieldset><p class="il-small">Changing the project or evidence clears the review and practice approval. Review the updated version again.</p></section>
        <section class="il-card il-wide il-release" aria-labelledby="il-release-title"><div><p class="il-step">07 / Release rehearsal</p><h3 id="il-release-title">The last step belongs to a person.</h3><p>This prepares a release handoff. It cannot publish, run a deploy, change access or approve future work. In a real project, the owner reviews the exact version and uses the established release process.</p><p class="il-small">For PointCast: scoped branch → independent review → owner approval → merge → deployment checks → production verification. Your draft does not skip any step.</p></div><div><fieldset id="il-deploy-checks" disabled><legend>Practice release gate</legend><div class="il-checks">{deployLabels.map((label, i) => <label><input type="checkbox" data-deploy={i} /><span>{label}</span></label>)}</div><label for="il-reference">Practice approval reference <small>5–200 characters · no names</small></label><input id="il-reference" data-field="approvalReference" maxlength="200" placeholder="Draft v1 / review note A / owner role" /><button class="il-button il-secondary" type="button" id="il-record-approval" disabled>Record practice approval</button></fieldset><p id="il-approval-state" class="il-state" aria-live="polite">No practice approval recorded. Nothing has been deployed.</p></div></section>
      </div>
      <section class="il-export" aria-labelledby="il-export-title"><div><p class="il-kicker">Leave a useful trail</p><h3 id="il-export-title">Take your handoff with you.</h3><p>Download at any stage. Share it only after checking the contents. Exports are local files, not submissions.</p></div><div class="il-actions"><button id="il-export-md" type="button" class="il-button">Download Markdown</button><button id="il-export-json" type="button" class="il-button il-outline">Download JSON</button><button id="il-reset" type="button" class="il-reset">Clear this draft</button></div><p id="il-download-status" role="status"></p></section>
    </section>
    <footer class="il-footer"><p>Make something small. Learn something real. Leave it easier for the next person.</p><div><a href="/communications-lab/">More educational briefs</a><a href="/intern.json">Current program status</a><a href="/internship-lab/program.json">Workflow JSON</a><a href="/bot-money/">Money Lab</a></div><small>PointCast / Written and built with Codex / October 19, 2026</small></footer>
  </div>
  <script>
    import { mountInternshipLab } from '../../scripts/internship-lab.mjs';
    const root = document.getElementById('internship-lab');
    if (root) mountInternshipLab(root);
  </script>
</BlockLayout>
